# Question 1
### Basic String Indexing

Given the DNA sequence `"ATCGATCG"`, write code to:
* Print the first nucleotide
* Print nucleotides from position 2 to 5 (inclusive)
* Print the last three nucleotides
<br>

# Question 2
### String Slicing with Protein Sequence

Using string slicing with `protein_sequence`, extract and print:
* The first 3 amino acids
* The last 4 amino acids
* Every second amino acid
<br></br>

# Question 3
### Demonstrating String Immutability

Demonstrate string immutability by trying to modify a character in the sequence "AGCT". Write code showing both:
* The incorrect way (trying to modify directly)
* The correct way (creating a new string)
<br></br>

# Question 4
### Finding Middle Character

Using string indexing, access and print the middle nucleotide in the sequence `"ATCGA"`
<br></br>

# Question 5
### Advanced Slicing

Using the sequence `"AATTCCGG"`, use string slicing to:
* Print all nucleotides except the first two
* Print all nucleotides except the last two
<br></br>
